From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:06:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Train the DIMM termination
 and the read ODT window

Two settings that the MRC of the Lenovo firmware trains and the NRI
left fixed (the MRC of a ThinkPad W541, read in its code):

- the termination of the DIMMs (its DIMM ODT step): with two DIMMs a
  channel RTT_NOM among 120, 60 and 40 ohms, then RTT_WR among 120 and
  60, each tried on all the ranks of the channel with the read and
  write margins measured, the MRC's tests and scale, and kept if it
  beats the one that was set by twice the threshold of the per-byte
  settings. Before the per-byte settings, which centre again. The JEDEC
  init wrote fixed values at every boot, a fast boot included: the
  chosen ones are now in sysinfo and in the saved training, and the
  JEDEC init writes those (60 and 60 until a training chooses);
- the read ODT window of each byte (its turnaround step, after the
  round trip step): the delay of the ODT and of the sense amplifiers
  from the receive enable, then how long they stay on. configure_mc()
  sets -2 and 7 qclks for every byte, the MRC leaves 0 to 3 and 3 to 4
  on the W541. The MRC weighs a later or shorter window as less power;
  these take the narrowest within one step of the widest eye and of the
  one that was set. On the W541 the package and DRAM power (RAPL) are the
  same with it as with the wide window, at rest and under load.

Both under HASWELL_NRI_OPT_PARAMS. The saved training changes layout,
so the boards train once more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ib6ad67504025a7b1062a7cf2b13c26f597829e86
